  "note": "Recto page in two parts. The top (y 0.138-0.415) is the tail of the Example 1.5 panel carried over from p014: a #dbdcde grey panel [0.1129, 0.1377, 0.6859, 0.4146] holding blocks n=1..n=5 (three prose stretches and two displayed equations), with the thin plain cyan #00adef bar on the inner (left) edge and the wide 'EXAMPLE 1.5' white-on-cyan label bar on the outer edge at x 0.696-0.738; those span the whole width of the panel so they and the panel blocks are marked `full`. Below the panel the page is GENUINELY two-column: section 1.7's prose and equations (blocks n=6..n=12) set in a narrow LEFT column x 0.097-0.545, with Fig. 1.8 (block n=13) and its cyan caption filling a RIGHT column x 0.546-0.873. Block n=8 is set wholly in italic (the statement of the superposition principle), which is why it alone carries font serif-italic. Section heading '1.7 FORCES BETWEEN MULTIPLE CHARGES' (n=6) is grey #6d6e71 at 1.45x body and is placed `full` because it starts in the left column but is the head of the whole section. The figure's left edge at x 0.546 is where its own ink begins; the q2/O labels are the leftmost parts. No footer_rule. Folio '15' in a pale cyan box in the outer margin; '2022-23' recorded as running_header."
